-- =========================
--  AutoCandyFarm (register-safe rewrite)
--
--  Fixes in this version:
--    * Void self-heal: hiding is refused when no real floor is found, the
--      hide point is validated, a watchdog rescues the character from the
--      void, and repeated hide deaths disable hiding for the rest of the round.
--    * "attempt to index nil with 'CharacterAdded'": LocalPlayer is awaited
--      (up to 2 minutes) and every signal is attached through a fresh,
--      pcall-protected lookup, so a queued rejoin loader can never hard-error.
--    * Death while shooting: a revenge fling now waits for the shot to end,
--      blocks the combat loop, and keeps flinging the murderer after respawn.
--    * Stacked execution: every root mover (tween, hide hold, fling, teleport
--      shoot, teleport gun) is mutually exclusive and every loop is bound to
--      the instance token + worker id, so two copies cannot fight the root.
--    * Duplicate execution: the live copy holds a heartbeat lease in getgenv.
--      A second execution now prints a notice and exits without touching the
--      first (set getgenv().__mm2candy_force = true first to replace it).
--    * Opening snap: as soon as the round's first candy is visible, the root
--      teleports straight to it once, then resumes the normal tween farming.
--      A per-round serial guard makes the snap strictly one-shot.
--    * Register pressure: state lives in tables and self-contained systems are
--      scoped in do-blocks, keeping the main chunk well under the 200-local
--      "out of local registers" limit.
--
--  Home toggles the farm. Config, Candy and P.api are exposed as before.
-- =========================

